lem says \"may use only the Python standard library\". List comprehension etc. fine.\n\nI'll produce code with comments? Keep minimal.\n\nOne more thought: The matrix might be sparse? In the given examples, many zeros. But we handle all.\n\nAlright, final answer should be a JSON object.\n\nWe'll write:\n\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    matrix = payload['matrix']\\n    idf = payload['idf']\\n    vector = payload['vector']\\n    result = []\\n    for col in range(len(idf)):\\n        total = 0.0\\n        for row in range(len(vector)):\\n            total += vector[row] * matrix[row][col] * idf[col]\\n        result.append(total)\\n    return result\"\n}\n\nBut need to escape newlines and quotes properly. In JSON, newline becomes \\n, double quote becomes \\\". So the string should have \\n for newlines. Also ensure no trailing spaces.\n\nI'll construct the string.\n\nDouble-check: The response must not have any preamble or trailing text. It must be exactly the JSON object.\n\nSo final."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1053,"completion_tokens":5006,"total_tokens":6059,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4889},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1053},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}